18 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating interactions between a tumor cell and a CAR-NK cell. The tumor cell, labeled on the left, interacts with the CAR-NK cell on the right through various receptors and signaling pathways. Key components include NCR, NKG2D, CD16, DAP10, DAP12, and PI3K. The process leads to the recruitment of macrophages and dendritic cells, and the induction of cytotoxicity.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a macrophage's interaction with a solid tumor cell. It shows several processes: enhancing phagocytosis, M2 to M1 macrophage polarization, recruiting and activating T cells, targeting the extracellular matrix, and activating NK and cytotoxic T cells while reducing Treg cells. The graphic includes labels and arrows indicating the progression and signaling pathways involved in these immune responses.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
